<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="work" class="doc-h2">Work (dependency order)</h2>
<ol class="doc-body">
    <li><strong>RemoteDB allowlist + object resolve</strong> (#2325, #2343) — <strong>DONE 2026-08-29</strong>. <code>postgresql|postgres|pg</code> in allowlist; <code>from_context($c)</code> for Catalyst callers.</li>
    <li><strong>Named PG connect</strong> (#2326) — <strong>DONE 2026-08-29</strong>. <code>db_production_postgres</code> returns a live handle on schema. Do not print the password.</li>
    <li><strong>Compare PG listing + Accounting namespace</strong> (#2327, #2328) — <strong>NEXT</strong>. Separate the Maria path; do not teach SHOW TABLES to PostgreSQL.</li>
    <li><strong>Create the first PG database from compare</strong> (#2329) after D1. Then IA <code>provision_site</code> (#2330).</li>
    <li><strong>Deploy one Accounting Result</strong> (#2331). Then D2 for purchase-order tables (#2332).</li>
</ol>
<p class="doc-info"><strong>Caller rule (locked 2026-08-29):</strong> never call Moose accessors on <code>$c-&gt;model('RemoteDB')</code> directly. Use <code>Comserv::Model::RemoteDB-&gt;from_context($c)</code> or <code>Controller::RemoteDB::_remote_db($c)</code>. Do not <code>extends 'Catalyst::Model'</code> on this class — it collides with Catalyst's class-level <code>config</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body">ACCPG todos #1795–1801 stay on InventoryAccounting. This plan does not author the Maria→PG row clone. It only gives compare a PG connection and a way to create the empty (or Result-deployed) database those todos need. Umbrella schema todo <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2280">#2280</a> comments now point here for the PG half of G1.</p>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="decisions" class="doc-h2">Open decisions</h2>
<table class="doc-table">
    <thead><tr><th class="doc-th">#</th><th class="doc-th">Decision</th><th class="doc-th">Resolution</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">D1</td>
            <td class="doc-td">How the first PG database is born</td>
            <td class="doc-td">OPEN — (a) compare CREATE DATABASE empty, then deploy every <code>Schema::Accounting</code> Result; or (b) one-time <code>accounting_template</code> DB from those Results, then keep <code>provision_site</code> TEMPLATE clone. Do not run <code>accounting_template.sql</code> by hand. Decide before #2329.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">D2</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Inventory* / purchase-order tables: Maria Ency vs site PG</td>
            <td class="doc-td">OPEN (measured 2026-09-24) — same as ACCPG D2. PO Result classes exist only under <code>Ency::Result::Accounting::InventoryPurchaseOrder</code> (+ Line) on Maria. <code>Schema::Accounting</code> has no PO sources. Receive/create run on Maria via <code>Purchasing::receive_po</code>. Do not Create Table PO onto site PG until this is decided. User still owns the move-vs-stay call.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="handoff" class="doc-h2">Handoff: schema → main → InventoryAccounting</h2>
<ol class="doc-body">
    <li>Review the schema worktree diff. Commit on <code>schema</code> only after that review.</li>
    <li>Merge <strong>schema into main from the primary checkout</strong> <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2</code>: <code>git merge --no-ff schema</code>. Never <code>git switch main</code> inside this worktree. Do not merge main back into schema just to clear “1 behind.”</li>
    <li>Continue CoA/AI/provision on InventoryAccounting (:4001). Pull/merge <em>main into that worktree</em> when you need these schema commits — not the other way around in a loop.</li>
</ol>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

